// Background rules.
// Start at 0 and use 5 lines, and each block is spaced apart on multiples of 10.
// Example shows that the meaning of each row:
// 
//	{80}{1008}       //Index into the description message file
//	{81}{94}         //Index into the effect message file
//	{82}{DWF DWM}    //The list of race-gender combinations for which the background is legal (list of codes is after this example)
//	{83}{400}        //How much money the background gives the character
//	{84}{6076 8263}  //The list of item prototype numbers separated by spaces (it should be left blank unless items are supplied)
// 
// If third line is left empty, all combinations can use the background. Otherwise the three letter codes are:
//
//	HUF - human female
//	HUM - human male
//	DWF - dwarf female
//	DWM - dwarf male
//	ELF - elf female
//	ELM - elf male
//	HEF - half elf female
//	HEM - half elf male
//	GNF - gnome female
//	GNM - gnome male
//	HAF - halfling female
//	HAM - halfling male
//	HOF - half orc female
//	HOM - half orc male
//	HGF - half ogre female
//	HGM - half ogre male
//	NPC - any NPC can use this background, regardless of their race or gender
//	ANY - anyone can use this background (same as blank line, included for clarity)
//

